data.description:
A small island, roughly 15 square miles in area, that hosts a bustling city with a population of around 5 million inhabitants. This vibrant metropolis features a diverse array of buildings and neighborhoods, including residential areas, shopping districts, educational institutions, sports facilities, bodybuilding gyms, and parks. The city is well-connected with a network of roads, highways, and a light rail system, allowing residents to navigate easily.

In this unique setting, the average adult inhabitants are about 9 to 10 inches tall, living in a world filled with structures designed for their size. For them, the towering "giants" are beings that appear to stand between 25 to 60 feet tall to the diminutive denizens. These giants, while not inherently malicious, have a tendency to accidentally cause chaos in the city, often uprooting buildings or carrying off tiny inhabitants out of curiosity or playfulness.

The tiny residents have adapted to their environment, creating a rich culture and community life.

